# madeintaha.com — Taha Mahmoodi portfolio

Static, self-contained personal portfolio. No build step, no runtime dependencies.
Everything (fonts, images, icons, GSAP) is vendored locally, so it deploys to any
static host and works offline.

## Run locally

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
# open http://localhost:8000
```

Or just open `index.html` in a browser.

## Deploy

Drop the whole folder on any static host:

- **Netlify / Vercel / Cloudflare Pages** — point it at this directory, no build command.
- **GitHub Pages** — push to a repo, enable Pages on the root.
- **Any web server** — copy the files to the web root.

Point `madeintaha.com` at the host once deployed.

## Structure

```
index.html          markup + content
css/style.css        design system (light + dark), all sections, responsive
js/main.js           theme toggle, reveals, magnetic buttons, count-up (no scroll listeners)
js/vendor/           GSAP + ScrollTrigger (hero parallax)
fonts/               Cabinet Grotesk + General Sans, self-hosted woff2
img/                 brand art (hero, about, work tiles) + icons/
```

## Swapping in real project images

The three featured work tiles (`img/tile-brand.jpg`, `tile-product.jpg`,
`tile-packaging.jpg`) are art-directed brand visuals in your palette, standing in
for the real deliverables. Replace them with actual Figma exports / screenshots at
roughly 1200x1000 (featured) to make the work section literal. The featured cards
currently link to the contact section; point them at case-study pages when those exist.

## Design notes

- Palette: warm paper, deep petrol-teal ink, coral accent (extracted from your CV brand).
- Type: Cabinet Grotesk (display) / General Sans (text).
- Motion respects `prefers-reduced-motion`. Theme respects `prefers-color-scheme`
  and remembers a manual toggle in `localStorage`.
